fer to fundamental care practices provided to all individuals, including those who are unable to eat or drink normally.", "ACUERDOS:Acuerdos refer to agreements made among healthcare professionals, patients, and families regarding treatment decisions, especially in complex cases.", "MODELOS CULTURALES:Modelos culturales refer to the cultural frameworks that influence healthcare practices and decision-making processes in different societies.)<|COMPLETE|>", "UNIVERSIDAD DE BARCELONA:The University of Barcelona is an educational institution where Begoña Román teaches.", "DIEGO GRACIA:Diego Gracia is a professor who advocates for a deliberative process in clinical nutrition decision-making.", "COMITÉ DE ÉTICA DE LOS SERVICIOS SOCIALES DE CATALUÑA:The Ethics Committee of Social Services in Catalonia oversees ethical practices in social services.", "COMITÉ DE BIOÉTICA DE CATALUÑA:The Bioethics Committee of Catalonia addresses ethical issues in healthcare and bioethics.", "LEY GENERAL DE SANIDAD:The General Health Law regulates health rights and services in Spain.", "CONSTITUCIÓN ESPAÑOLA:The Constitución Española is the Spanish Constitution that serves as the foundational legal framework for the country. It delineates the fundamental rights and freedoms of individuals in Spain, ensuring the protection of various rights, including the right to health protection. This constitution plays a crucial role in safeguarding the liberties and well-being of the Spanish populace.", "PROCESO DELIBERATIVO:The deliberative process involves structured discussions to make ethical decisions in clinical settings."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}